{
  "configuration_id": "config_002",
  "reason": "Evidence: We have only one completed experiment (config_012: RNA-only, singleprofile, pca_n2000 → 48.5% acc), so uncertainty is high across all design axes. The most fundamental question for a multimodal profiling study is whether adding the image modality provides any signal beyond RNA alone. Question: config_002 (multimodal, singleprofile, pca_n2000, resnet50, concat fusion, no aggregation) is the minimal-change extension of config_012—it keeps the same RNA encoder, same profile setting, and adds only a standard image encoder (ResNet50) with the simplest fusion (concat). This directly isolates the contribution of image information. Why this is the best next experiment: If multimodal outperforms the RNA-only baseline, it justifies further investment in image encoder choice, aggregation, and fusion. If it does not, it redirects the search toward RNA-side improvements (encoder, multiprofile). No other single experiment reduces uncertainty about this core design decision as cleanly, and it avoids changing multiple axes simultaneously."
}

